+
+/**
+ * Sorts the branches of a loop by how they absorb neighboring iterations. A
+ * branch `P S R`, with S a star that accepts every character of the other
+ * items, absorbs them into S:
+ *
+ * - With one branch, one iteration matches every concatenation of
+ *   iterations: in `x1 x2 ... xn`, P matches as in x1, R as in xn, and S
+ *   consumes everything between. Lookarounds in P and R see the same
+ *   absolute positions as in x1 and xn.
